---
title: Baked Chicken Breasts
image: https://www.gimmesomeoven.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/Oven-Baked-Chicken-Breast-Recipe-3.jpg
time required: 35 minutes
course: Main Course
source: https://www.gimmesomeoven.com/baked-chicken-breast/
prep time: 20 minutes
tags: chicken, gluten free
servings: 4
cook time: 15 minutes
cuisine: American
---

> Check the label of your chicken breasts before the initial brine, because if your chicken is pre-brined, you should skip this step.

Fill a large mixing bowl with @water{2%cups} of lukewarm water and @kosher salt{1/4%cup}. Stir to combine until most of the salt is absorbed. 

Add @water{2%cups}(or a few ice cubes) to lower the temperature of the water so that it is cool to the touch. 

Add the @chicken breasts{4}(boneless skinless, pounded to even thickness) and let them sit in the mixture to brine for ~{15%minutes}, or you can also cover the bowl and refrigerate for up to ~{6%hours}. 

Remove the chicken breasts from the brine, rinse them with cold water, then pat them dry with paper towels.

Heat the oven. Preheat oven to 450°F.

Place the chicken breasts in a single layer in a #baking dish{}. 

In a separate #small bowl{}, whisk @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, and @smoked paprika{1/2%tsp} until combined. 

Brush @melted butter or olive oil{} onto the chicken evenly. Sprinkle the seasoning mixture evenly over the chicken. Flip chicken and repeat on the other side.

Bake for ~{15-18%minutes}, or until the chicken is cooked through and no longer pink.

> Cooking time will depend on the thickness of the chicken breasts, so I recommend using a cooking thermometer to know exactly when the chicken is fully cooked. The thickest part of the breast should measure 165°F. 

> If you want the chicken to be a little bit browned and crispier on top, you can turn the broiler on high for the final 3-5 minutes of the cooking time and broil the chicken until it is cooked through and golden on top. Keep a close eye on the chicken, however, so that it does not overcook and/or burn.

Once the chicken is cooked, remove the pan from the oven, transfer the chicken to a clean plate, and loosely tent the plate with aluminum foil. Let the chicken rest for at least ~{5-10%minutes}.